  },
  "design": [
    "Cancellation-aware output sits below the 64 KiB buffer. Each delegated file write is at most 65,536 bytes and checks cancellation/interruption first.",
    "The underlying file closes even when cancellation aborts buffered flush. Staging failure removes the private file.",
    "Owner publication remains atomic and uncancellable once authoritative commit begins. Inventory, health and drop patching are unchanged.",
    "A single model serialization or filesystem write can still take time. This is a byte checkpoint bound, not a cancellation-time guarantee."
  ],
  "tests": {
    "command": "mvn -q -Dmaven.repo.local=\"$PWD/target/structure-m2\" -DargLine=\"-Djava.io.tmpdir=$PWD/target/structure-offline-history-tmp\" -Dtest=StructureOfflineSaveTest,StructureOfflineHistoryStagingTest test",
    "exit_code": 0,
    "tests": 15,
    "failures": 0,
    "errors": 0,
    "skipped": 0,
    "coverage": [
      "Version 8/9 save-byte compatibility, current survival state, close/cancel cleanup and failed atomic replacement.",
      "Nine history/integration tests cover stale history, model mismatch, full rollback, no undo after failure and actual StructureMenu retry.",
      "Eight 16-resolution checker models encode more than 128 KiB. Cancellation before the second raw write occurs before history progress. A positive private byte count is at most 65,536; prior save bytes and live edits stay unchanged, and the private file is removed.",
      "One 32-resolution checker model exceeds 128 KiB. Thread interruption during its raw output stops after at least 64 KiB but before 128 KiB, preserves the interrupt flag until test cleanup, makes no history progress, preserves prior save bytes and removes its private file."
    ],
    "initial_fixture_correction": "An initial assertion assumed exactly 65,536 bytes but BufferedOutputStream flushed 63,354 bytes. The corrected assertion requires positive bytes at most 65,536; the final 14 tests passed. A final interruption case was added; all 15 final tests passed.",
